# Course HTML Lessons

Theory materials are HTML files in the `theory/` folder of each module.

## Resource Links

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../../assets/css/course.css">
<script src="../../assets/js/course.js" defer></script>
```

Adjust the number of `../` segments based on file nesting depth.

## HTML Lesson Structure

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Lesson Title</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../assets/css/course.css">
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Lesson Title</h1>
  <p>Theory content...</p>
  <div class="note">Important note</div>
  <div class="exercise">Self-check exercise</div>
  <pre><code>code example</code></pre>
  <script src="../../assets/js/course.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
```

## Content Rules

- Language: English.
- Short paragraphs, simple words.
- One topic per lesson.
- Code examples from engineering and mathematics.
- Use `.note`, `.warning`, and `.exercise` blocks from `course.css`.
